Dave Thaler said:

@Thomas Fossati: on slide 9 you say "Lead Attester takes responsibility for signing the Verifier nonce"... how does that protect against some replay in between the Lead and Device Attesters?

ultimately, the security of the composite attester relies on the evidence collection process being implemented correctly (i.e., there are no interposers on the collection path) and certain assumptions about the collected evidence being true (e.g., that the device state did not change between capture and retrieval).  Provided all of this is captured in the attestation measurements, the Verifier/PR can evaluate that metric and make a decision
